{
  "id": "ss.env.menu",
  "name": "Home screen \u2014 the hive at night",
  "description": "The premise as one picture: a whole horizon that glows and signals, and one cold sealed thing down at the left that does not. Pheromone spires rise in three depth bands, a Chorus burns low on the right, and scent drifts up off the ground everywhere except around the survivor. Authored at 1280x720 and baked at 2x so the cover-scale the menu applies does not magnify it \u2014 the camera shows ~1.56 device pixels per world unit, and a smaller sheet turned this into mush. Composed for the menu it sits behind \u2014 the middle is deliberately the darkest, quietest part of the frame so the title, cast row and buttons stay readable over it, with all the incident pushed to the edges and the floor.",
